{
  "dom_id": "step-q146208",
  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,8)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0.45, & y=4 \\\\ 0.55, & y=6 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSuppose $X$ and $Y$ are discrete random variables. Find the conditional variance $\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=8]$ given that the conditional probability mass function ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,8)$ is shown above and the corresponding conditional expected value is ${\\mu }_{Y|8}=5.1.$",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that the conditional variance of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=x] & =\\text{E}[(Y-{\\mu }_{Y|x})^{2}\\,|\\,X=x] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=x]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2} \\\\  & =[{\\sum }_{y}{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=8] & =[{\\sum }_{y}{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,8)]-{\\mu }_{Y|8}^{2} \\\\  & =[(4)^{2}\\cdot 0.45+(6)^{2}\\cdot 0.55]-(5.1)^{2} \\\\  & =7.2+19.8-26.01 \\\\  & =0.99.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
